# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anchoring rules — read before adding a pattern.
#
# A pattern with no leading slash and no interior slash matches at EVERY depth, and on Windows
# core.ignorecase=true it matches case-insensitively too. That combination is how a bare
# `artifacts/` silently swallowed src/JuiceShop.Automation.Utility/Artifacts/ — a SOURCE folder.
# Its two files were never committed on any branch, `git status` stayed clean, MSBuild does not
# read .gitignore so local builds passed, and the only symptom was CS0246 in CI.
#
# Rule: leave a pattern unanchored only if it must genuinely match at every depth. Anything that
# is a repo-root output gets a leading slash.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build output. Unanchored on purpose — one per project. `bin/` already covers bin/Debug,
# bin/Release, and the whole runtime artifact tree the tests write underneath it:
# bin/<cfg>/net10.0/artifacts/{traces,screenshots,videos,logs} and .../allure-results.
bin/
obj/

# Repo-root test output. `artifacts/test-results` is .runsettings' ResultsDirectory, which VSTest
# resolves relative to the directory holding the .runsettings file — this one, the repo root.
/artifacts/
*.trx

# VSTest's fallback results directory, created next to whichever project ran. Left unanchored
# because it can appear under any project.
TestResults/

# Allure. Raw results live under bin/ and are already covered. These only ever appear at the repo
# root — from `allure generate` locally, or the report action and history checkout in CI.
/allure-results/
/allure-report/
/allure-history/
/gh-pages/

# Playwright auth state — contains live session cookies and tokens
.auth/
**/playwright/.auth/

# IDE and local tooling
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude
.claude/
*.user
*.suo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
